#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157013 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "5f10a215-83bb-545a-a0e1-ce702f773e6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-7112" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ and the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ below, find the value of $x_2,$ the second component of $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/4f788e589f34c94ac03e11f7cee87f9af695af2a86d57a2e4630f07c30babb1e.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2,\\,\\mathbf{q}_3.$ \n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/cfa33ba159e0627ec7a7288e44249acd88e0037e285fa786888dfcc13e5d538c.png) where $x_i = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i}{\\mathbf{q}_i \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i}.$ \n\nComputing $x_2,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-4)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+6+8}{1+1+16} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157014 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "d7df79a9-2489-5fed-9e00-29890bd01f82" :question/math-academy-id "e-7113" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/5a56202f818d8b8d10dd06d5e4bd02ee0aabc2f16758ca64cb6dc416fb71075c.png) of $\\mathbb R^2,$ find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ if ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/d97e5bc94afc05532528354b82231eab87ca49ec72bd42879759c64c4165837d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2.$ \n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/1ba0b151abea3c5b1a050c6ff924f3718fcb045b063b1b47df7a73f9d15316c9.png) where $x_i = \\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i.$ Computing the components of $\\mathbf{x},$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-2-6=-8 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-4+3=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/51184680e9ec8b56a437334ca2a9281b1b364da2c35922839be13e545d92cec4.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b354047d-d921-5251-8048-7155b847509f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357650} {:answer/id #uuid "32a825ef-d817-5dfa-b570-539f7289bfe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357651} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa97402-e5a7-5f24-9fa6-6a10b5d24d79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357652} {:answer/id #uuid "3577c778-45c1-5e5f-9c2a-59a38870e981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}+1 \\\\ 1-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357653} {:answer/id #uuid "59780a65-0686-5308-ae83-3a9c09a2682d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59780a65-0686-5308-ae83-3a9c09a2682d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357654} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f157ac8-0538-5e2f-a79d-a1816e8f4298" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ecfc4989-ba47-5e5d-ab5f-597b5de37da2" :question/math-academy-id "q-102322" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]=\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]=1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b51cbc9-465b-573d-b720-d2a65d0aaf0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357657} {:answer/id #uuid "23ee76ce-f0bd-5ccf-aad9-749a8eaeff14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357658} {:answer/id #uuid "deb0d8de-131c-5913-b72c-eb6375f07c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357659} {:answer/id #uuid "29984e99-1ee9-541c-9957-a233bb839e81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357660} {:answer/id #uuid "95fd1f0b-65ed-5594-9788-2a8a333217f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29984e99-1ee9-541c-9957-a233bb839e81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357660} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ecbea9-2776-511f-b96a-68a144c5aa6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a10a6f4-6466-5b27-9f8e-862bce8849e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-102333" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $5{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x\\cdot {q}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4+0+3 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n5{x}_{2}=5\\cdot 7=35.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357662 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e8946b0-edb0-5dbf-a6e0-24085c6e25e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357664} {:answer/id #uuid "94cb1f2a-4b76-5c37-8f10-3df2d20faf2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357665} {:answer/id #uuid "7a1fce8e-56f1-5c68-a90d-b522c18a24f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357666} {:answer/id #uuid "32d37b97-1905-5f3a-951b-7508799b5c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357667} {:answer/id #uuid "02d6911f-3645-5beb-a97c-9513f2e65712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e8946b0-edb0-5dbf-a6e0-24085c6e25e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357664} :answer-field/id #uuid "2715a4c6-23e6-5bb6-a9c1-927f60f215d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4256b0ff-2ba2-5434-b86b-57b1a7c57a55" :question/math-academy-id "q-102337" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $5{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot (-4)+(-4)\\cdot 2}{{(-4)}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20-8}{20} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n5{x}_{1}=5\\cdot (-\\frac{7}{5})=-7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc6633d5-634a-5de8-9383-c71df457af53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357671} {:answer/id #uuid "5da04c4b-0d45-5643-b283-9d1b31340cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357672} {:answer/id #uuid "0796a34e-8f6e-5da2-a996-c174f9c1b19f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357673} {:answer/id #uuid "0021cee8-75b7-55dc-83ea-7d5433490442" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357674} {:answer/id #uuid "7081d8cc-9480-51ee-a2dc-0f47af20caf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0796a34e-8f6e-5da2-a996-c174f9c1b19f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357673} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4d19498-a07a-5b68-a9ff-a896f581e9a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36209143-148a-589e-bd6c-a0a79a189fea" :question/math-academy-id "q-102352" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $100{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}25 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 25+0\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot (-4)}{{25}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{25-12}{625+9+16} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{650} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n100{x}_{2}=100\\cdot \\frac{1}{50}=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9254ea79-8223-5408-88d8-673a1a9426d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155513} {:answer/id #uuid "9a11f5fe-02c8-5034-8236-308db1adc6aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155514} {:answer/id #uuid "eafb40be-422e-5447-b360-9b42915dc668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155515} {:answer/id #uuid "3152041d-ad44-53c3-90db-fd6824834ebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155516} {:answer/id #uuid "66b89f6d-b041-51bb-9e8a-5ac5cff8e506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9254ea79-8223-5408-88d8-673a1a9426d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155513} :answer-field/id #uuid "beea1ca6-15e0-5f29-aa27-ccc29bcf3761" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c2da7ca-24a0-572d-977f-07408d1bbebe" :question/math-academy-id "q-40291" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $26{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 2}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-2}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n26{x}_{1}=26\\cdot \\frac{7}{13}=14.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73754197-9df0-5f9e-8e68-798e0e8af72a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357678} {:answer/id #uuid "4bd79555-e120-5535-b5a1-4e4b9192ff28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357679} {:answer/id #uuid "d5296e84-2d19-5b31-8c90-adb5f54c536c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357680} {:answer/id #uuid "f183ec17-9e53-5099-90f6-6c9d8f4d941b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357681} {:answer/id #uuid "9c0efd41-43bc-5b50-8385-a83d37132725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bd79555-e120-5535-b5a1-4e4b9192ff28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357679} :answer-field/id #uuid "406fbe6f-cbd9-5883-b4ba-ea0f74d7b37d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d52318cf-590e-555c-bafa-19ac086a5c9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-40293" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]}$  of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}=-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{25}{\\sqrt{26}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}=-\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "107a1ac2-0019-5d7a-905a-5e8d42f29d55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357685} {:answer/id #uuid "0486cbc8-7667-5613-a544-9495d38a8ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357686} {:answer/id #uuid "183a08ec-af7c-57e0-b23e-2501443c5acc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357687} {:answer/id #uuid "cbdc191a-0db6-5f8e-93ba-008409d008d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357688} {:answer/id #uuid "4aba28ec-7841-5a76-9616-23c1ff88d805" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0486cbc8-7667-5613-a544-9495d38a8ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357686} :answer-field/id #uuid "75760990-5f31-57b3-97ba-b443b6edacd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dac20b74-113a-570f-b2db-aa2c08090e57" :question/math-academy-id "q-40401" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 57\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0+57\\cdot 7}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+399}{1+49} \\\\  & =\\frac{400}{50} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}_{1}}{2}=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357690 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06300a6b-bd04-5016-8397-5cd808e28ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357692} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ca6f8f-e7ab-57e1-b972-28b11b2674ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357693} {:answer/id #uuid "027cff53-b458-5365-9f96-3449780f79a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357694} {:answer/id #uuid "98dab1af-5e5d-565d-ace9-6340cc118d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357695} {:answer/id #uuid "b3887c32-2361-5a41-8b20-24819bdce57f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98dab1af-5e5d-565d-ace9-6340cc118d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357695} :answer-field/id #uuid "98853296-ef75-5709-97c4-8dc7e236856c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cea8b9f0-0696-5c6a-80c2-c39460b290e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-81103" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $15{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot (-3)}{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+12}{1+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n15{x}_{1}=15\\cdot \\frac{7}{5}=21.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65a1ba53-d9ca-5ff1-9f3d-9c4fc0989396" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294809} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbe921f-67d0-5706-a5c6-36b025c7070d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294810} {:answer/id #uuid "35cf3d11-b2c5-5e9f-acba-db3eb0fbcd21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294811} {:answer/id #uuid "0c319097-9c82-5855-844a-1c3b6a816381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294812} {:answer/id #uuid "93dc7b26-4f82-599a-a051-8216bdcf5712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93dc7b26-4f82-599a-a051-8216bdcf5712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294813} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b1e9640-f0e5-54fd-a3ed-9808ca7fd7ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "694ae25e-76dc-5254-b28a-52858f45659d" :question/math-academy-id "q-81106" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}}=-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}+\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{10}}=\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2360b739-5034-5408-9b57-0c2afbfc6c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357699} {:answer/id #uuid "8a758842-126e-59cf-adf7-cf26f67ed7ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357700} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7ae272-9a8e-536c-9318-070d3b7e7395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357701} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ad758e-7fa4-5faf-b091-69ba2accb8ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357702} {:answer/id #uuid "48216367-6101-5212-9268-4d44ae58e969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a758842-126e-59cf-adf7-cf26f67ed7ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357700} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef25aae2-1444-5782-a5dc-90f980b348c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c22da228-1825-58b8-9f3c-add207e837ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-81142" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $\\sqrt{6}{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x\\cdot {q}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}}+\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{6}}-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}{x}_{2}=\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}=6.\n$$"}]}
